\\ objdata.6502 - the objects' bank: the background objects' variants (tools/gendata.py), their bytes and
\\ the tables obj_events reads them by.

\\ The tables first, the same size on every track (padded to the most, gendata.py's ObjVariantsMax and
\\ EntriesMax), so the bank's code is at the same place on every track; the bytes last (ObjSlot, sprint.6502).

.ObjTabSlot                             ; the track's part (Phase 5, 3a)
\\ Each kind's first variant (kind 1 the slots' sprites, 2 the gates', 3 the barriers'), then per variant its
\\ width in bytes, height, flags (ObjMasked, ObjHasPrio) and where its bytes, mask and priority bits are

.ObjKindBase
    EQUB GenObjKindBase
.ObjW
    EQUB GenObjW
.ObjH
    EQUB GenObjH
.ObjFlags
    EQUB GenObjFlags
.ObjDataLo
    EQUB LO(ObjData + GenObjData)
.ObjDataHi
    EQUB HI(ObjData + GenObjData)
.ObjMaskLo
    EQUB LO(ObjData + GenObjMask)
.ObjMaskHi
    EQUB HI(ObjData + GenObjMask)

\\ The gates' and barriers' entries, one per transition (an instance from one frame to the next, or its
\\ first): its variant (from its kind's first), its runs (up to 3: where in the cars' bank's priority data,
\\ how many bytes; a first draw's every cell, a step's only each cell row's span of cells that change),
\\ their bits

.EntVar
    EQUB GenEntVar
.EntRuns
    EQUB GenEntRuns
.EntRunLo
    EQUB LO(PrioData + GenEntRunOff)
.EntRunHi
    EQUB HI(PrioData + GenEntRunOff)
.EntRunLen
    EQUB GenEntRunLen
.EntDataLo
    EQUB LO(ObjData + GenEntData)
.EntDataHi
    EQUB HI(ObjData + GenEntData)
.ObjTabSlotEnd
